{
  "_comment": [
    "Ground truth from the live JVM oracle (sigmastate-interpreter 6.0.2,",
    "scripts/jvm_serde_oracle/ErgoSerdeOracle.scala via",
    "`difftest --oracle --repro <tree_hex> --surface reduce`) for JIT cost of",
    "AND / OR / XorOf over boolean-collection literals -- issue #311.",
    "",
    "Derivation (sigmastate 6.0.x source):",
    " * ConcreteCollectionBooleanConstantSerializer.parse (data/shared/src/main/",
    "   scala/sigma/serialization/ConcreteCollectionBooleanConstantSerializer.scala:35-48)",
    "   rebuilds the packed 0x85 form as ConcreteCollection(BooleanConstant.fromBoolean(bit)...),",
    "   so the packed form is a wire optimisation only.",
    " * ConcreteCollection.eval (sigma/ast/values.scala:858-869) charges",
    "   ConcreteCollection.costKind = Fixed(20) (values.scala:907) once, then evalTo",
    "   on every item; each item is Constant.eval (values.scala:351-354) at",
    "   Constant.costKind = Fixed(5) (values.scala:380). Collection cost = 20 + 5*n.",
    " * AND.eval (sigma/ast/trees.scala:270-283): PerItemCost(10, 5, 32) over the",
    "   number of items its `while (i < len && res)` loop visited (prefix through",
    "   the first false), not the collection length.",
    " * OR.eval (trees.scala:199-212): PerItemCost(5, 5, 64) over the prefix",
    "   through the first true.",
    " * XorOf.eval (trees.scala:239-245): PerItemCost(20, 5, 32) over the full length.",
    " * PerItemCost.cost (sigma/ast/CostKind.scala:26-32): base + perChunk *",
    "   ((n - 1) / chunkSize + 1) -- one chunk at n = 0.",
    " * BoolToSigmaProp = Fixed(15); a Coll[Boolean] Constant (type 0x0d) is one",
    "   Constant node = Fixed(5) with no per-item charge.",
    "",
    "Each vector is a v0 ErgoTree (header 0x00) reduced with an empty context",
    "extension and no registers; `expected` is the oracle's verbatim",
    "`ACCEPT P:<sigma_hex>|<jit_cost>` line. `rust_before_fix` is recorded for",
    "the record only and is NOT an oracle."
  ],
